x & 2 x \\
-5 x & x
\end{array}\right]+\left[\begin{array}{ll}
y & 0 \\
0 & y
\end{array}\right] \\
& \therefore \quad\left[\begin{array}{cc}
\frac{1}{11} & \frac{-2}{11} \\
\frac{5}{11} & \frac{1}{11}
\end{array}\right]=\left[\begin{array}{cc}
x+y & 2 x \\
-5 x & x+y
\end{array}\right]
\end{aligned}\therefore \quad$ By the equality of matrices,
$\begin{array}{ll} 
& 2 x=\frac{-2}{11} \text { and } x+y=\frac{1}{11} \\
